  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Pegasus Diaries – The Private Papers of Major John Horward DSO\n£12.99\n\nLow stock, 3 remaining\nThe Pegasus Diaries - The Private Papers of Major John Horward DSO quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nJohn Howard & Penny Bates\n\nJohn Howard's name will forever be linked to the highly successful Pegasus Bridge assault by his glider-borne company of the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry. His men regarded him with awe and his courage and toughness were bywords. However this book reveals the human side of the man as well as providing a graphic account of the preparation, actual operation and aftermath of this iconic action.\n\nThe Pegasus Diaries is a book that will be enjoyed by men and women alike, presenting as it does a complex man often torn between his high sense of loyalty to his men and devotion to duty.\n\nPaperback, 198 pages, 32 black and white illustrations.\nISBN: 9781844158829\n\nRelated products\nMESOPOTAMIA 1914-15: EXTRACTS FROM A REGIMENTAL OFFICER’S DIARY\n£11.99 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre VIII\n£5.00 Add to cart\nChildren and War – A Bugle & Sabre Special\n£2.00 Add to cart\nThe Story of the Oxfordshire Yeomanry – Queen’s Own Oxfordshire Hussars 1798-1998\n£7.95 Read more\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
